  "heading": null,
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Axiom of Choice}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Axiom:\ngiven:\n. I, U is \\set\n. A(i__) is \\function:on{I}:to{\\power.set:of{U}}\nwhere:\n. forAll: i \"in\" I\n  then:\n  . exists: S is \\set\n    suchThat:\n    . S = A(i)\n    . S != \\empty.set\nthen:\n. exists: f(i__) is \\function:on{I}:to{U}\n  suchThat:\n  . forAll: i \"in\" I\n    then:\n    . exists: S is \\set\n      suchThat:\n      . S = A(i)\n      . f(i) \"in\"? S\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Axiom of Choice\"\n. description: \"Every set-indexed family of nonempty subsets of an ambient set\n                admits a choice function selecting one element from each member\n                of the family. This ambient-set formulation is equivalent over\n                ZF to the usual formulation for arbitrary set-indexed families.\"\nId: \"3f1ec40e-207c-431e-918e-7a8f4f23fa46\"",
